  "result": "I created `src/slugify.js` and `test/slugify.test.js`, and touched no other file. I could not run the tests: the shell tool needed approval and was denied, so the suite is unexecuted. I checked the expected values in the tests by hand against the code instead.\n\n- **`src/slugify.js`** exports `{ slugify }` as specified. It lowercases, strips diacritics via NFD normalization, turns each run of non-`a-z0-9` characters into one `-`, and trims dashes from both ends. With `maxLength`, it cuts at the last dash that fits, or cuts hard if the first word is too long. It throws a `TypeError` for non-strings.\n- **`test/slugify.test.js`** uses `node:test` and `node:assert`. It covers the five examples from your spec, plus accent handling, dash collapsing, empty input, the `TypeError`, and the `maxLength` edge cases: a dash landing exactly on the limit, no trailing dash, and a hard cut of one long word.\n\nTo run them: `npm test` from the repo root.",
